1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,650
I'm Surekha Jaknalli, from team Impromptu, with Rahul Rajpoot and Vivek Chaturvedi.

2
00:00:05,650 --> 00:00:08,646
Impromptu helps people write better prompts.

3
00:00:08,646 --> 00:00:13,139
My part, Task Harness, makes sure the AI's answers can be trusted.

4
00:00:13,939 --> 00:00:17,015
AI is usually right, but sometimes quietly wrong.

5
00:00:17,015 --> 00:00:22,853
In our test, the cheapest Claude model got 6 out of 30 invoices wrong, and nobody was warned.

6
00:00:22,853 --> 00:00:29,318
Impromptu asks the AI to keep every fact and constraint, but today nothing checks that it actually did.

7
00:00:30,118 --> 00:00:38,626
Task Harness checks every AI answer with plain code: is each value really in the source, is it from the right place, do the numbers add up.

8
00:00:38,626 --> 00:00:44,013
If not, the AI gets one retry with the exact problem, and otherwise a person reviews it.

9
00:00:44,013 --> 00:00:52,214
With the harness, the cheapest model got 30 out of 30 correct, with zero silent errors, about 38 times cheaper than the biggest model.

10
00:00:53,014 --> 00:00:58,710
Our next step is to plug the same gate into Impromptu, so every prompt rewrite gets checked.

11
00:00:58,710 --> 00:01:02,487
Nothing lost: every name, number, date and every not is kept.

12
00:01:02,487 --> 00:01:03,540
Nothing invented.

13
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:05,583
And the chosen skill is followed.

14
00:01:05,583 --> 00:01:12,393
If a check fails, the AI retries once, and the user sees a clear warning instead of a silently changed prompt.

15
00:01:12,393 --> 00:01:16,355
Impromptu improves the question; Task Harness checks the answer.
